# App Router Standards

Rules:

- `src/app` owns routes, layouts, metadata, viewport, globals and page composition.
- Do not place visual section implementation directly in `src/app`.
- Do not put business logic or large static data in `page.tsx`.
- `page.tsx` should only compose sections in order.
- Keep `layout.tsx` responsible for global fonts, metadata and accessibility shell.
- New public routes need metadata and SEO review.
- Keep `/` static unless a real dynamic requirement appears.
- Use Server Components for static sections.
- Isolate forms, embeds and animation wrappers as Client Components.
- Any App Router strategy change requires an ADR.
